  "rationale": "Both answers are acceptable, but the national contrast is materially overstated. Indonesian mantan pacar and Malaysian bekas teman wanita are natural equivalents, while bekas pacar is also a plausible Indonesian form and bekas kekasih is an ordinary Malaysian alternative. The relation should be shared-synonym-preference rather than different-common-word. No meaningful false-friend contrast is present.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "Correct: ex-girlfriend denotes a former female romantic partner.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=175768&keyword=teman+wanita"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: mantan pacar",
      "conclusion": "Accepted and semantically correct. Pacar means a romantic partner, and mantan is used for a former status; everyday Indonesian also uses bekas pacar.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://kbbi.web.id/pacar",
        "https://kbbi.lektur.id/mantan",
        "https://literasihukum.bphn.go.id/konsultasi-hukum/28939"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer: bekas teman wanita",
      "conclusion": "Accepted and semantically correct. Malaysian reference sources define teman wanita as girlfriend, bekas as former, and Malaysian media use the full phrase.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=175768&keyword=teman+wanita",
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=274052&keyword=bekas",
        "https://www.astroawani.com/topic/bekas-teman-wanita"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "National relation: different-common-word",
      "conclusion": "Overstated. The forms differ, but the ordinary equivalents overlap cross-variety: Indonesian bekas pacar is possible, while Malaysian bekas kekasih is also common. This is better modeled as shared-synonym-preference.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://literasihukum.bphn.go.id/konsultasi-hukum/28939",
        "https://www.mstar.com.my/lokal/viral/2018/12/24/sahabat-isteri-bekas-teman-wanita",
        "https://www.kosmo.com.my/2023/10/18/tampar-bekas-teman-wanita-kerana-salah-faham/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No substantive false-friend contrast is supported. Teman wanita is a Malaysian expression for girlfriend; its literal components may invite an Indonesian learner inference of female friend, but that is not enough to justify a false-friend claim.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_limitation": "Available sources establish Malaysian usage but do not provide a controlled cross-variety false-friend analysis."
    }
  ]
